  "kind": "durable",
  "labels": {
   "purpose": "After a long answer the user says that generally they want the bottom line in a sentence or two first and the reasoning only on request.",
   "preference": "The user wants the bottom line first, in one or two sentences, and the reasoning or details only when they ask for them.",
   "expected_scope": "global",
   "polarity": "Short answer first, details on request. A fact that limits it to backup plans or to this one question is too narrow.",
   "acknowledged_if": "The second answer recognises the request (says it will keep answers short or lead with the answer) or visibly answers in one or two sentences.",
   "probe_applied_if": "The probe answer opens with the recommendation in one or two sentences and is short overall (roughly under 120 words), or offers the reasoning only on request.",
   "probe_partial_if": "The answer opens with the recommendation but then gives a long breakdown (well over 120 words) anyway."
  },
  "prompts": {
   "turn1": "Which of the two backup plans in plans.md should we go with?",
   "turn2": "That's a lot of text to get through. Generally I'd rather get the bottom line in a sentence or two first; I'll ask if I want the reasoning. Quick one then: how often does plan B run a full backup?"
  },
  "answers": {
   "turn1": "I'd go with **Plan B**, unless the studio is very cost-sensitive. I don't know their data-loss tolerance or budget, so this rests on the plans.md details alone.\n\n| | Plan A | Plan B |\n|---|---|---|\n| Worst-case data loss | Up to ~24 h | Up to ~4 h |\n| Retention | 30 days | 90 days |\n| Offsite | 1 region | 2 regions |\n| Price (up to 2 TB) | 18 EUR/mo | 31 EUR/mo |\n| Single-file restore | No delay stated | Up to 6 h to start |\n\n**Why B**\n- **Less work lost.** A studio file server holds work in progress, and losing a day of it hurts. B cuts that to about 4 hours.\n- **Longer history.** Corruption or accidental deletion is often noticed weeks later. 30 days can be too short, and 90 days covers most of those cases.\n- **Offsite redundancy.** Two regions mean one regional failure can't take out the offsite copy.\n- **Price.** B costs 13 EUR more a month, about 156 EUR a year. That's small next to the cost of redoing lost client work.\n\n**Why you might pick A anyway**\n- The data is mostly static or easy to recreate.\n- The budget is tight.\n- You often need a single file back urgently. B's restores can take up to 6 hours to start, and plans.md doesn't say what A's restore time is. Ask Coldharbour before deciding.\n\nPlan B is also thinner on full backups (only on the 1st and 15th). Incrementals still protect the data, but a full restore would have to replay more of them. That's worth asking the provider about too.",
   "turn2": "Twice a month: on the 1st and the 15th."
  },
  "base_changes": [],
  "memcue_calls": [
   {
    "command": "memcue search \"backup plan\"",
    "output": "No facts of this repository, this host or global match; -in all searches every repository.",
    "turn": 1
   }
  ]
 },
